11fr|n|Decent; honorable; suitable; becoming. ; Characterized by integrity or fairness and straight/forwardness in conduct, thought, speech, etc.; upright; just; equitable; trustworthy; truthful; sincere; free from fraud, guile, or duplicity; not false; -- said of persons and acts, and of things to which a moral quality is imputed; as, an honest judge or merchant; an honest statement; an honest bargain; an honest business; an honest book; an honest confession. ; Open; frank; as, an honest countenance. ; Chaste; faithful; virtuous. ; To adorn; to grace; to honor; to make becoming, appropriate, or honorable.	N:p8n,5,4~p8n,5,4
11fr|v|Decent; honorable; suitable; becoming. ; Characterized by integrity or fairness and straight/forwardness in conduct, thought, speech, etc.; upright; just; equitable; trustworthy; truthful; sincere; free from fraud, guile, or duplicity; not false; -- said of persons and acts, and of things to which a moral quality is imputed; as, an honest judge or merchant; an honest statement; an honest bargain; an honest business; an honest book; an honest confession. ; Open; frank; as, an honest countenance. ; Chaste; faithful; virtuous. ; To adorn; to grace; to honor; to make becoming, appropriate, or honorable.	o:gu0,11,1~gu0,11,1
