11fv|n|Honor; honorableness; dignity; propriety; suitableness; decency. ; The quality or state of being honest; probity; fairness and straightforwardness of conduct, speech, etc.; integrity; sincerity; truthfulness; freedom from fraud or guile. ; Chastity; modesty. ; Satin flower; the name of two cruciferous herbs having large flat pods, the round shining partitions of which are more beautiful than the blossom; -- called also lunary and moonwort. Lunaria biennis is common honesty; L. rediva is perennial honesty.	a:wax,13,3~wax,13,3	V:1vj4,26,4;1biz,11,3~1vj4,26,4;1biz,11,3	n:97,3,15~97,3,15	N:1p3i,48,29;16x8,32,9;1xbe,22,3;16x4,21,8~1p3i,48,29;16x8,32,9;16x4,21,8;1xbe,22,3
