11g0|n|A mass of hexagonal waxen cells, formed by bees, and used by them to hold their honey and their eggs. ; Any substance, as a easting of iron, a piece of worm-eaten wood, or of triple, etc., perforated with cells like a honeycomb.	a:28h5,145,4;1ifn,45,5;3b2,28,12;1xdf,14,1~3b2,28,12;1ifn,45,5;28h5,145,4;1xdf,14,1	v:1xdf,49,11~1xdf,49,11	n:20t,53,1;2156,17,4;19yi,4,5~19yi,4,5;2156,17,4;20t,53,1	N:14qw,67,5;27ab,58,8;27ad,54,1;1ltq,53,3;1wul,33,3;ld7,33,3;2dmx,11,1~27ab,58,8;14qw,67,5;ld7,33,3;1ltq,53,3;1wul,33,3;27ad,54,1;2dmx,11,1
